{"t": 1794105632.6207075, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*reports-api 502 \u2014 root cause found and fixed*\n\nCause: upstream ledger (2026.11) added a `currency` field to every row. `reports/export.py` builds its CSV with a fixed field list `[id, amount]`, so `csv.DictWriter` raised `ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'` and the export endpoint failed (502). CloudWatch `/ecs/reports-api` (eu-west-1) shows this at 2026-11-04 19:02:11.\n\nFix: added `currency` to the CSV fieldnames in `reports/export.py`. Verified locally: rows with `currency` export correctly, and older rows without it still export with a blank currency.\n\nAction: deploy the updated reports-api. After deploy, confirm exports succeed and check the 5xx rate. No data loss expected."}, "ok": true}
